## Status — 2026-10-14 (implemented, local commit)

Done. In-app debug logging with no ADB:

- `DebugLog.kt` (new): thread-safe, in-memory ring buffer (1000 lines), Android-free (JVM-testable). API: `DebugLog.d(tag, msg)`, `state` (StateFlow<List<String>>), `snapshot()`, `clear()`, `enabled`, `KEY_PHRASE = "WCAST_DEBUG"`.
- `SettingsStore.kt`: added `debugLogsEnabled` pref (`debug_logs_enabled`).
- `SettingsActivity.kt`: new **Debug** section → "Debug logs" toggle + "View debug logs" nav row (chevron). Flag initialized & wired to `DebugLog.enabled`.
- `DebugLogActivity.kt` (new) + manifest: read-only viewer with Select-all / Copy / Clear top-bar icons + long-press selection; live-updates via `collectAsState`.
- `MainActivity.kt` / `SettingsActivity.kt`: `DebugLog.enabled` seeded from prefs on create.
- `SpeechController.kt`: keyed timing around generation & playback (issue 02) — stream start, synth start/result (renderMs), synth done/error, play start (gapMs vs previous chunk end = the inter-paragraph delay), utterance ended, look-ahead frontier, pause/resume. Existing `Log.d("WcastTTS", …)` left intact.
- `AGENTS.md`: "Debug logging (in-app, no ADB)" section — route all new debug output through `DebugLog.d`, key-phrase `WCAST_DEBUG` so call sites are grep-strippable.
- `DebugLogTest.kt` (new): 4 tests (disabled no-op, formatted line, bounded buffer drops oldest, clear) — all pass.

Not done (per ticket scope): no disk persistence; logs reset on process death. Clicking the body text relies on Android's selection handles (no programmatic select-all), so the Select-all icon copies the full buffer to the clipboard.

